<div class='mb-6'>
  <p class='title'>Line Chart Hollow Markers</p>
  <p class='mb-2 text-sm'>
    A hollow marker is a transparent fill plus a colored ring:
    <code>pointBackgroundColor</code> transparent and <code>pointBorderColor</code> set by the
    caller. The ring color is a default (white), not a lock — this is how a suppressed or
    estimated value is drawn apart from measured ones (#1065).
  </p>

  <%= render Bali::Chart::Component.new(
      type: 'line', data: {
        labels: ['Jan', 'Feb', 'Mar', 'Abr', 'May', 'Jun', 'Jul'],
        datasets: [
          {
            label: 'Measured',
            data: [12, 19, 14, 23, 17, 25, 21]
          },
          {
            label: 'Suppressed (<5)',
            data: [2, nil, 3, nil, 2, nil, 1],
            pointBackgroundColor: 'rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)',
            pointBorderColor: 'rgba(100, 116, 139, 0.90)',
            pointBorderWidth: 2
          }
        ]
      }
  ) %>
</div>

